IMPORT prelude

-- Shared nouns of the Legislation Interpretation Act 2021 (South Australia): the kinds of thing the rules of reading talk about.
-- Nouns only: no rule and no assertion lives here.
-- Each type is used by more than one module.

§ `Nouns`

-- Section 3 and most sections speak of "an Act or a legislative instrument".
DECLARE `Kind of enactment` IS ONE OF
    `an Act`
    `a legislative instrument`

-- Sections 9, 10 and 13 speak of an individual, a body corporate and the other things the Act calls an entity.
DECLARE `Kind of entity` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`
    `a partnership`
    `an unincorporated body`
    `another kind of entity`
